EXT. GLACIER CREVASSE - DAY

A blue slot in the ice, forty feet deep, walls ribbed like the inside of a throat. Wind whistles across the lip.

INGRID HALVORSEN, forties, a mountaineer in a red jacket, dangles from a rope at the crevasse edge, kicking for purchase. SOLANGE RENARD, thirties, her partner, lies flat on the ice above, the rope wrapped around her gloves. DAG, fifties, their guide, plants an ice axe a few feet back and hauls on the line.

SOLANGE
I've got you!

INGRID
You don't!

SOLANGE
She's slipping, Dag!

DAG
Both of you, shut up and haul.

Ingrid swings her boot at the wall. The ice bites. She hangs, breathing.

INGRID
Tell me when she's got the axe in.

DAG
Axe is in.

Solange pulls. Ingrid rises one foot, then two. She grabs the lip with a gloved hand. She looks up at Solange. She looks at Dag.

INGRID
Pull.

They pull. She crawls onto the ice, gasping. Nobody speaks. Dag unwraps the rope from Solange's hands, finger by finger.
